1.3. A population moving towards gender parity
Like other countries on the European continent, the population of the Principality of Monaco has had a
gender balance that has been moving towards parity for several decades.
Figure 4. Breakdown of the resident population by gender in 2025
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses
Women account for 50.8% of Monaco’s resident population in 2025, i.e. 19,730 women for 19,127 men.
Figure 5. Change in the breakdown of the resident population by sex from 1951 to 2025
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses
Since 1951, the breakdown between men and women has tended to balance out. The gender gap was
11.4 percentage points in 1951 and 5.0 points in 1990. In 2025, it is down to just 1.6 points.
