 2025 Population census – May 2026 7
1.4. An ageing resident population
The age pyramid of Monaco’s residents has an atypical shape, characterised by a high proportion of people
aged 45 to 64.
Figure 6. Resident population pyramid in 2025 (number of people)
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses
Before age 30, the pyramid shows a very balanced distribution between women and men, with stable
numbers ranging from 150 to 200 people per age and sex.
The 50-70 age group records the highest numbers, with at least 220 people per age and sex, reaching up
to 383 men at age 62 compared with 324 women at age 59, which highlights a higher proportion of men in
these ages.
From age 70 onwards, women become the majority in the resident population: they account for 54.1% of
people aged 70 and over.
There are 60 centenarians in 2025, i.e. less than 0.2% of the population.
