 2025 Population census – May 2026 8
Table 2. Resident population by age group and sex in 2025
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses
In 2025, nearly 5,800 people, or 14.9% of the population, are aged 75 and over. This is the age group in
which the gap between women and men is the widest, with women accounting for 16.3% of the female
population compared with 13.5% for men.
At the same time, residents under the age of 16 account for 15.1% of the population, a proportion that is
almost identical to that of people aged 75 and over.
Figure 7. Change in the mean age of residents by sex from 2000 to 2025
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses
Despite a slight decrease for the first time since 2000, the average age of residents is 47.2 years in 2025
(47.7 years for women compared with 46.5 years for men). It has increased by 2.5 years since 2000.
The gender gap has narrowed significantly since 2000, falling from 3.3 years in favour of women to 1.2 years
in 2025.
