Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses
With 9,333 people in 2025, or nearly a quarter of the resident population, Monegasques remain the leading
nationality in the Principality since 2023. They are followed by the French (8,270) and the Italians (7,559).
The British number more than 3,000, whil e the Swiss, Russian and Belgian communities each account for
between 1,000 and 1,300 nationals.
Cypriots, Maltese and Israelis are the nationalities in the top 30 with the highest proportion of multinationals,
with seven residents out of ten. The Danes have the highest proportion of men (58.5%), while the Filipinos
have the highest proportion of women (73.0%).
Monegasques and French have a relatively close mean age, at 45.4 years and 46.3 years respectively.
Ukrainians have the youngest average age, at 34.6 years, while Turks have the highest, at 57.0 years.

