 2025 Population census – May 2026 20
Methodological notes
The register -based census involves bringing together the various existing databases and information
systems, namely:
 Data on Monegasque nationals from the Civil Status and Nationality Department of Monaco City
Hall;
 Data on residence permits issued by the Police Department (Direction de la Sûreté Publique -
DSP);
 Data on pupils attending school in Monaco from the Department of Education, Youth and Sport
(Direction de l'Éducation Nationale de la Jeunesse et des Sports - DENJS);
 Data on births in Monaco from the Civil Status and Nationality Department of Monaco City Hall.
The remaining population (foreign minors aged 3 to 17 not attending school in the Principality, foreign
children born outside Monaco between 2023 and 2025) is estimated on the basis of 2016 census data.
Distribution of the resident population in 2025
Source: Monaco Statistics – 2025 Population census
The aim is to obtain a database containing as much common information as possible between the various
registers. The variables selected for each observation are as follows:
- age;
- gender;
- the number of different nationalities;
- nationality or nationalities (from 1 to 4, corresponding to the maximum number of multiple
nationalities observed for a single resident in the source files used);
- family situation.
