--- page 21 ----------------------------------------------------
 2025 Population census – May 2026 21
 Monegasque nationals
The Civil Status and Nationality Department of the Monaco City Hall updates the “sommier” (register of
Monegasque nationals), which includes information such as each person's address. Only Monegasque
nationals declaring that they reside in the Principality have been included in this database for the
census.
The family situation of Monegasques is known only for the complete population, without any details
concerning residence. Therefore, for each age/gender combination, the percentage of residents is applied
to the breakdown by family situation.
 Foreign nationals over the age of 18
The DSP issues a residence permit to any foreign national aged 16 or over wishing to stay in Monaco for
more than three months or wishing to take up residence here. To avoid double counting with the register of
schoolchildren, only foreign residents aged 18 and over holding a residence permit have been
considered in the census.
 Foreign nationals aged 3 to 17
Foreigners aged 3 -17 attending school in Monaco
The DENJS has a database of all pupils attending school in the Principality of Monaco in the public and
private sectors (under contract and not). To avoid double counting, with the residence permit register, only
resident pupils of foreign nationality aged between 3 and 17 inclusive have been included in this
database for the census.
Foreigners aged 3 -17 not attending school in Monaco
Foreign children aged 3 to 17 not attending school in the Principality were estimated using the percentage
of children not attending school in the Principality observed in the 2016 Census.
The population aged 3 to 5 was isolated, given the significant variation in this rate at these ages, due to the
gradual entry of children into nursery school: 25.3% at 3 years, 13.6% at 4 years and 7.9% at 5 years. The
rate observed in 2016 for the population aged 6 to 10 (11.5%) was applied to estimate foreign minors aged
6 to 10 not attending school in the Principality, and the same for those aged 11 to 17 (17.7%).
 Children under 3
The Civil Status and Nationality Department of the Monaco City Hall is also responsible for registering life
events occurring in the Principality, such as births. To count children aged 0 to 2 of foreign nationality born
and living in the Principality (res ident father or mother), only births occurring in Monaco between 2023
and 2025 have been considered in this database for the census.
Finally, the number of foreign children born outside Monaco between 2023 and 2025 was estimated based
on the proportion of foreign children aged under one and born outside Monaco recorded in 2016.
The nationality of these children was determined on the basis of the distribution observed among 6-16 year
olds, the closest known population in age. Only the 30 most common combinations of nationalities were
considered.

