 2025 Population census – May 2026 22
 Breakdown of residents by district
Housings
Two data sources are used for housing data:
- Address database of the Department of Forward Studies, Urban Planning and Mobility (Direction de
la Prospective de l'Urbanisme et de la Mobilité - DPUM), which lists all the buildings in Monaco and
the number of private and state-owned housing units in each;
- Export of all state-owned housing from the State Property Authority.
This second source replaces the data relating to public housing in the DPUM address database.
Residents
To estimate the number of residents per district, the distribution of housing units in 2025 and the size of
households per district established in the 2016 census were used.
By multiplying the number of housing units by the size of households, a projected population is obtained,
from which the distribution by district is determined.
The estimated resident population per district is obtained by applying this breakdown to the actual
population of the 2025 census (38,857).
